Test that the echo controller restarts for recording and keeps what it knows of the room

WebRTC's audio processing and AEC3 with its patches 0010 and 0011: an echo controller that
can restart for recording is kept (RestartEchoController creates none) and one that cannot
is made anew; AEC3 with a headset (7 s of the other side's sound, only the room's noise at
the microphone) lets the first 0.5 s after RestartForRecording through within 3 dB, and a
new AEC3 at the same point holds them at least 6 dB lower, so the test tells the two
apart. Built in again: the library shows only its own API.

